WEBVTT

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:09.369
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Friday, 24 April. Are we all on? Teams is doing that thing where half the faces disappear.</v>

00:00:09.949 --> 00:00:14.150
<v Aisha Begum>I'm here. Only just, mind. Traffic on the ring road was ridiculous.</v>

00:00:16.629 --> 00:00:23.629
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, traffic on the ring road got me as well. Sat looking at the same drain cover for ten minutes.</v>

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.390
<v Fiona Doyle>Lovely bit of sightseeing, that.</v>

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:34.229
<v Grace Liu>I'd swap you. The heating in the portakabin is either tropical or completely off. Apparently we've gone tropical this morning.</v>

00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:37.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Ah, the luxury office package.</v>

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.990
<v Priya Raman>Can you hear me? My headset's— hang on. There.</v>

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:47.579
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, got you. Right, finished stuff first, then what we're actually agreeing.</v>

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:56.770
<v Aisha Begum>I tested the line 3 barrel yesterday and it's all fine now. That's finished, nothing new off the back of it.</v>

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:02.899
<v Hannah Price>Good. That was the one still showing in yesterday's conversation, wasn't it?</v>

00:01:03.979 --> 00:01:09.930
<v Priya Raman>And I tested the Compressed Air Dryer yesterday and it's all fine now. That test is done.</v>

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:15.599
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers. The sensor recalibration on the Compressed Air Dryer is still separate though, yeah?</v>

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:20.579
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, different bit. Yesterday was the functional test, not the recalibration.</v>

00:01:21.599 --> 00:01:26.849
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha, can you recalibrate the sensors on the Compressed Air Dryer this morning? Normal priority.</v>

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:32.459
<v Aisha Begum>Yep, I'll recalibrate the sensors on the Compressed Air Dryer this morning.</v>

00:01:34.269 --> 00:01:37.069
<v Fiona Doyle>Normal priority, this morning. Not reopening yesterday's test.</v>

00:01:38.719 --> 00:01:40.469
<v Aisha Begum>Exactly, yeah. Two separate things.</v>

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:44.890
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, what about the seals on the main water valve?</v>

00:01:46.829 --> 00:01:54.879
<v Marcus Hale>I'll replace the seals on the main water valve. It's not an emergency but don't let it slip, that one. I'll take it.</v>

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.000
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Marcus. Agreed, that's yours.</v>

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:04.900
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, not a drop-everything job, but not one to quietly forget either.</v>

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:15.949
<v Priya Raman>Just on water, I noticed the Site Water System was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down. Just an observation, not raising another job.</v>

00:02:17.689 --> 00:02:26.439
<v Fiona Doyle>Same sort of thing: noticed the turbine one gas valve was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down. Nothing outstanding from that.</v>

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:30.740
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, both observations only. Not adding those as actions.</v>

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:37.449
<v Priya Raman>And still waiting on parts for the Air Compressor 1, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. That's still blocked, not something we're committing to do today.</v>

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.400
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep. No change there.</v>

00:02:49.039 --> 00:02:56.039
<v Sarah Okafor>Priya Raman, can you do the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet by the end of the week? Normal priority.</v>

00:02:58.069 --> 00:03:04.719
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, no, I haven't got the capacity to take that. Don't put it against me and assume it's covered.</v>

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:12.479
<v Fiona Doyle>Sarah, could you take the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet instead, then? Same end-of-week deadline, normal priority.</v>

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:20.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, I'll take them. I'll do the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet by the end of the week. Normal priority.</v>

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:28.030
<v Grace Liu>And pre-use is still pre-use, obviously. End of the week isn't permission to use anything unchecked.</v>

00:03:29.229 --> 00:03:34.479
<v Sarah Okafor>Absolutely. It's Friday today anyway, but yes, understood. Those checks are mine, not Priya Raman's.</v>

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:40.900
<v Sarah Okafor>Grace, can you sort the training records for the new starters this morning? No rush.</v>

00:03:42.169 --> 00:03:46.370
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I'll sort the training records for the new starters this morning.</v>

00:03:47.819 --> 00:03:51.319
<v Fiona Doyle>Sorry, talking over you— no rush, but still this morning?</v>

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:58.610
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes. No need to drop everything this instant, but this morning is still the deadline.</v>

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.900
<v Grace Liu>Fine by me. That's clear.</v>

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:10.909
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha, can you also grease and check the bearings on the feedwater pump? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:17.720
<v Aisha Begum>Yep, I'll grease and check the bearings on the feedwater pump. I'll take that as well.</v>

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:22.699
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, that wording's about right. Doesn't need the blue lights and sirens.</v>

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:28.069
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Not an emergency, but it does need doing. Aisha's got it.</v>

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:34.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha, could you write up the near miss at the Main Outfeed Conveyor on Friday as well?</v>

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:41.990
<v Aisha Begum>Um, no, sorry. With those two I've just accepted, I can't take the write-up as well. It'll get squeezed out.</v>

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:50.670
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough. Grace, can you take that instead: write up the near miss at the Main Outfeed Conveyor on Friday?</v>

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:58.889
<v Grace Liu>Yes, I'll write up the near miss at the Main Outfeed Conveyor on Friday. Take Aisha off that one; it's mine.</v>

00:05:01.319 --> 00:05:05.870
<v Fiona Doyle>And Friday there means today, just so nobody reads it as next Friday.</v>

00:05:08.269 --> 00:05:10.720
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, today. Grace has accepted that one.</v>

00:05:12.959 --> 00:05:18.910
<v Sarah Okafor>Han, can you investigate the pressure drop on the GT2 water valve for Monday? That's fairly important.</v>

00:05:21.279 --> 00:05:26.879
<v Hannah Price>Yep, I'll investigate the pressure drop on the GT2 water valve, due Monday. Understood, fairly important.</v>

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:33.810
<v Priya Raman>That's separate from the main water valve seals, just to keep the two straight?</v>

00:05:35.949 --> 00:05:40.850
<v Hannah Price>Yes. Mine's the pressure-drop investigation on the GT2 water valve, not the seal replacement.</v>

00:05:41.569 --> 00:05:48.920
<v Fiona Doyle>There's also the collection from Kestrel Hydraulics Leeds, the replacement parts for the Boiler Safety Relief Valve. That's still needing someone.</v>

00:05:51.389 --> 00:05:58.740
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll go to Kestrel Hydraulics Leeds to pick up the replacement parts for the Boiler Safety Relief Valve tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:02.829
<v Marcus Hale>Tomorrow? You've remembered that's Saturday, yeah?</v>

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:07.769
<v Sarah Okafor>I have, sadly. Tomorrow, Saturday the 25th, at 9:30. I'll do the collection.</v>

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:12.790
<v Fiona Doyle>Okay, Sarah for that. Tomorrow at 9:30, understood.</v>

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:21.379
<v Grace Liu>One gap, though. The risk assessment for work on the Injection Moulding Line 3 needs updating. That's not done.</v>

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:28.459
<v Sarah Okafor>Anyone able to take updating the risk assessment for work on the Injection Moulding Line 3?</v>

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:35.350
<v Grace Liu>I can't take that on with the records and the near-miss write-up. Raising the gap, not volunteering, sorry.</v>

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:38.660
<v Aisha Begum>I can't pick it up either.</v>

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:45.000
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Nobody's taking that one. It remains unallocated; let's not make it look covered when it isn't.</v>

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:52.139
<v Hannah Price>And the line 3 barrel test being finished doesn't mean that risk assessment's sorted. Different thing.</v>

00:06:53.389 --> 00:06:58.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Quite. Test done, risk assessment update still needs an owner. No commitment on that today.</v>

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:05.759
<v Priya Raman>Nothing else from me. And you can still hear me, so that's a personal best for Teams.</v>

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:09.709
<v Marcus Hale>Don't say that out loud. It'll hear you.</v>

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:17.649
<v Grace Liu>At least if it cuts out, I'll still have the sound of this heater attempting take-off.</v>

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:20.899
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, we'll leave it there. Thanks, everyone. Cheers.</v>
